Fonts. `.design-sync/fonts/` holds IBM Plex Sans and IBM Plex Mono
(Copyright IBM Corp., https://github.com/IBM/plex) and Instrument Serif
(published by Instrument, https://github.com/Instrument/instrument-serif),
Latin subsets taken from Google Fonts. All three are under the SIL Open Font
License 1.1, whose text is in each project named above. They are shipped so
that a design built from the component bundle renders in the console's real
faces rather than in a fallback; the console itself names the families and
embeds nothing.

Case material. The runs under `docs/use-cases/` were worked on public
forensic challenges other people made:

  - Ali Hadi's Digital Forensic Challenge Images, for every `dfir-*` case.
    https://www.ashemery.com/dfir.html
  - Belkasoft's BelkaCTF series, for the `belkactf` cases. The task text in
    an edition's `challenges.md` is quoted from the challenge board as the
    site states it. https://belkasoft.com/ctf

No evidence file from either source is in this repository, and none should be
added: the images are large, their authors publish them, and each case README
says where to get them. What is here is the swarm's own record of working
them — the board, the ledger, the trace, the report and the screenshots. That
record is this project's work and the licence above covers it. The scenarios,
the questions and the challenge text it quotes are not, and stay with the
authors named here.

